div.p:
742
.  To direct an attack to the right, left, or rear the soldier will change front as quickly as possible in the most convenient manner, for example: 1. To the right rear, 2. Cut, 3. DOWN;
1. To the right, 2. LUNGE;
1. To the left, 2. THRUST, etc.

754
.  To provide against attack from the right, left, or rear the soldier will change front as quickly as possible in the most convenient manner, for example, 1. To the left rear, 2. Parry, 3. HIGH;
1. To the right, 2. Parry, 3. RIGHT, etc.
